# SHA-256 of the upstream ontologies the ontology-frontiers work was measured against.
#
# Recorded from the copies vendored on research/zd-fiber-antisymmetry-lemma-20260731 at
# 6bd961cc46, so these checksums describe the exact bytes the published numbers came from.
# Sizes there: uberon.owl 95,887,167 B  cl.owl 66,012,941 B  ro.owl (see below).
#
# Regenerate with fetch_upstream_ontologies.sh, then:
#   sha256sum -c scripts/research/ontology-frontiers/UPSTREAM_ONTOLOGIES.sha256
#
# A checksum mismatch means upstream moved, NOT that the work is wrong — OBO ontologies
# are re-released continuously. It means the numbers must be re-measured or the old
# release pinned by URL before they are quoted again.
938f51e7c3fc9fcbe5a2863eb346da8033737e568af5836958891c4c6bfb1192  artifacts/ontology-frontiers/multi-ontology/downloads/uberon.owl
6abe12f1569d077507e03c1ad0168ebbb9ed725973a7eddba8ab3b9aeaf7a68d  artifacts/ontology-frontiers/multi-ontology/downloads/cl.owl
a9f644d4a865747e0b4aba7ca3f19aac1e0b072cab89e24a2e476df3abb10aaf  artifacts/ontology-frontiers/multi-ontology/downloads/ro.owl
